IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sfa-core`

-- Securities and Futures Act 2001 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, SSO informal consolidation
-- "version in force from 29/6/2026 to 20/10/2026" (a rendering, not the official text).
-- Part 13 Division 1 Subdivision (2) -- ss 240AA, 240AB and 240A: the product highlights sheet, its exemptions, and the debenture issuance programme. LAYER 1: the law, objectively.
--
-- Reading a result (the rule of 2026-10-29): JUST TRUE is yes; JUST FALSE is "the TEXT says no in its own words"; NOTHING is "the text does not say".
-- A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE. Every "no" branch carries `-- FALSE-kind (...)`, every "not covered" branch `-- NOTHING-kind (...)`.
-- Where an answer of another function is an input (a MAYBE BOOLEAN), only JUST TRUE counts as the fact being shown; JUST FALSE and NOTHING are both read as "not shown", never as a no.
-- The Act's "such requirements as the Authority may prescribe" are INPUTS (a fact). Section 262(3) (asset-backed securities) is outside this range: seam S5.

-- inert (reason 1), lines 38888-38888: s 240AA(5) opening words "In this section": the definitions are each encoded in their own function.
-- inert (reason 1), lines 38992-38992: s 240AB marginal heading: not operative.
-- inert (reason 1), lines 39027-39027: s 240A marginal heading: not operative.
-- inert (reason 2), lines 39089-39091: s 240A(8): the Authority may by regulations prescribe how the provisions of this Subdivision apply to an offer referred to in subsection (1) or (2); a regulation-making power, whatever it prescribes is not in this text.

§ `s 240AA: the product highlights sheet`

DECLARE `s 240AA action` IS ONE OF
    `s 240AA(1) make the offer`
    `s 240AA(2) publish or disseminate the document`

-- s 240AA(1): the bar. "unless" is a closed gate; the bar is limited by its own wording to a person who makes an offer of relevant securities, in or with a prospectus or profile statement that complies with section 240.
-- src:38829 | 240AA.—(1) A person must not make an offer of any relevant
-- src:38830 | securities or securities‑based derivatives contracts, being an offer that
-- src:38831 | is made in or accompanied by a prospectus or profile statement that
-- src:38836 | complies with section 240, unless the prospectus or profile statement
-- src:38837 | is accompanied by a product highlights sheet in respect of the offer —
-- src:38839 | (a) that complies with such requirements as the Authority may
-- src:38840 | prescribe by regulations made under section 341; and
-- src:38842 | (b) a copy of which is lodged with the Authority.
@ref s 240AA(1) (src:38829-38842)
GIVEN
    `the person makes an offer of securities or securities-based derivatives contracts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person make an offer of securities or securities-based derivatives contracts (as section 239(6) says when a person makes an offer)?
    `the securities or contracts offered are relevant securities or securities-based derivatives contracts` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function `s 240AA(5) "relevant securities or securities-based derivatives contracts" the securities or contracts are relevant` answer for the securities or contracts offered? (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE, or NOTHING if you do not know.)
    `the offer is made in or accompanied by a prospectus or profile statement that complies with section 240` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the offer made in, or accompanied by, a prospectus or profile statement that complies with section 240?
    `the prospectus or profile statement is accompanied by a product highlights sheet in respect of the offer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the prospectus or profile statement accompanied by a product highlights sheet in respect of the offer?
    `the product highlights sheet complies with the requirements the Authority has prescribed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the product highlights sheet comply with the requirements the Authority has prescribed by regulations made under section 341?
    `a copy of the product highlights sheet is lodged with the Authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a copy of the product highlights sheet lodged with the Authority?
    `the person is exempted from the requirements in section 240AA` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function `s 240AB(1) and (2) the person is exempt from the requirements in section 240AA` answer for the person? (JUST TRUE if the person is exempt; any other answer is read as the exemption not being shown.)
    `this Subdivision applies to the offer` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function `s 239A(1) and (2), s 239(8) and Subdivision (4): this Subdivision applies to the offer` answer for the offer? (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE, or NOTHING if you do not know.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
-- FORK F10 (see NOTES.md, Fork register)
`s 240AA(1) the person must not make the offer` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the person makes an offer of securities or securities-based derivatives contracts`)
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A person must not make an offer of any relevant securities or securities-based derivatives contracts"  -- SPLIT-SITE (i)
        IF `the securities or contracts offered are relevant securities or securities-based derivatives contracts` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "an offer of any relevant securities or securities-based derivatives contracts"  -- SPLIT-SITE (i)
        IF (NOT `the offer is made in or accompanied by a prospectus or profile statement that complies with section 240`)
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "being an offer that is made in or accompanied by a prospectus or profile statement that complies with section 240"  -- SPLIT-SITE (i)
        IF `the person is exempted from the requirements in section 240AA` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "exempt any person or class of persons from all or any of the requirements in section 240AA"
        IF `the prospectus or profile statement is accompanied by a product highlights sheet in respect of the offer` AND `the product highlights sheet complies with the requirements the Authority has prescribed` AND `a copy of the product highlights sheet is lodged with the Authority`
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the prospectus or profile statement is accompanied by a product highlights sheet in respect of the offer (a) that complies with such requirements as the Authority may prescribe by regulations made under section 341; and (b) a copy of which is lodged with the Authority"
        IF `this Subdivision applies to the offer` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "then this Division does not apply to that offer"
        IF (`this Subdivision applies to the offer` EQUALS NOTHING) OR (`the securities or contracts offered are relevant securities or securities-based derivatives contracts` EQUALS NOTHING)
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the answer of another provision (the disapplication of this Subdivision, or the meaning of relevant securities) was not worked out
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

@ref s 240AA(1) (the prohibition as a rule) (src:38829-38842)
GIVEN
    `the person` IS A Party @desc Who is the person who makes the offer?
    `what section 240AA(1) answers for the person` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function `s 240AA(1) the person must not make the offer` answer for the person? (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE, or NOTHING if you do not know.)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 240AA action`
`s 240AA(1) the person shall not make the offer without a product highlights sheet` MEANS
    IF `what section 240AA(1) answers for the person` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN PARTY `the person`
         SHANT `s 240AA(1) make the offer`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY `the person` BECAUSE "the offer was made without the product highlights sheet section 240AA(1) requires; section 240AA(4) makes that an offence"
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- s 240AA(2): the bar on publishing a document that resembles a product highlights sheet. "if the document resembles" is a failed "if" (reading (a)); "unless" is a closed gate.
-- src:38846 | (2) A person must not publish or disseminate, whether in Singapore
-- src:38847 | or elsewhere, any document relating to any offer or intended offer of
-- src:38848 | any relevant securities or securities‑based derivatives contracts, being
-- src:38849 | an offer that is, or an intended offer that will be, made in or
-- src:38850 | accompanied by a prospectus or profile statement that complies with
-- src:38851 | section 240, if the document resembles or may otherwise be confused
-- src:38852 | with a product highlights sheet, unless the person is required to do
-- src:38853 | so —
-- src:38855 | (a) under any written law or rule of law, or by any court, in
-- src:38856 | Singapore;
-- src:38858 | (b) under the laws and practices of, or by any court in, any
-- src:38859 | foreign jurisdiction; or
-- src:38861 | (c) by any listing rules or other requirements of any approved
-- src:38862 | exchange or overseas exchange.
@ref s 240AA(2) (src:38846-38862)
GIVEN
    `the person publishes or disseminates a document, whether in Singapore or elsewhere` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person publish or disseminate a document, whether in Singapore or elsewhere?
    `the securities or contracts of the offer or intended offer are relevant securities or securities-based derivatives contracts` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function `s 240AA(5) "relevant securities or securities-based derivatives contracts" the securities or contracts are relevant` answer for the securities or contracts of the offer or intended offer? (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE, or NOTHING if you do not know.)
    `the document relates to an offer or intended offer made in or accompanied by a prospectus or profile statement that complies with section 240` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the document relate to an offer that is, or an intended offer that will be, made in or accompanied by a prospectus or profile statement that complies with section 240?
    `the document resembles or may otherwise be confused with a product highlights sheet` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the document resemble a product highlights sheet, or might it otherwise be confused with one?
    `the person is required to publish or disseminate it under any written law or rule of law, or by any court, in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person required to publish or disseminate the document under any written law or rule of law, or by any court, in Singapore?
    `the person is required to publish or disseminate it under the laws and practices of, or by any court in, any foreign jurisdiction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person required to publish or disseminate the document under the laws and practices of, or by any court in, any foreign jurisdiction?
    `the person is required to publish or disseminate it by any listing rules or other requirements of any approved exchange or overseas exchange` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person required to publish or disseminate the document by any listing rules or other requirements of any approved exchange or overseas exchange?
    `the person is exempted from the requirements in section 240AA` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function `s 240AB(1) and (2) the person is exempt from the requirements in section 240AA` answer for the person? (JUST TRUE if the person is exempt; any other answer is read as the exemption not being shown.)
    `this Subdivision applies to the offer` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function `s 239A(1) and (2), s 239(8) and Subdivision (4): this Subdivision applies to the offer` answer for the offer? (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE, or NOTHING if you do not know.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
-- FORK F11 (see NOTES.md, Fork register)
`s 240AA(2) the person must not publish or disseminate the document` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the person publishes or disseminates a document, whether in Singapore or elsewhere`)
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A person must not publish or disseminate, whether in Singapore or elsewhere, any document relating to any offer or intended offer"  -- SPLIT-SITE (i)
        IF `the securities or contracts of the offer or intended offer are relevant securities or securities-based derivatives contracts` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any offer or intended offer of any relevant securities or securities-based derivatives contracts"  -- SPLIT-SITE (i)
        IF (NOT `the document relates to an offer or intended offer made in or accompanied by a prospectus or profile statement that complies with section 240`)
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "being an offer that is, or an intended offer that will be, made in or accompanied by a prospectus or profile statement that complies with section 240"  -- SPLIT-SITE (i)
        IF (NOT `the document resembles or may otherwise be confused with a product highlights sheet`)
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the document resembles or may otherwise be confused with a product highlights sheet"  -- SPLIT-SITE (i)  -- MARGINAL-READING (a)
        IF `the person is exempted from the requirements in section 240AA` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "exempt any person or class of persons from all or any of the requirements in section 240AA"
        IF `the person is required to publish or disseminate it under any written law or rule of law, or by any court, in Singapore` OR `the person is required to publish or disseminate it under the laws and practices of, or by any court in, any foreign jurisdiction` OR `the person is required to publish or disseminate it by any listing rules or other requirements of any approved exchange or overseas exchange`
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the person is required to do so (a) under any written law or rule of law, or by any court, in Singapore; (b) under the laws and practices of, or by any court in, any foreign jurisdiction; or (c) by any listing rules or other requirements of any approved exchange or overseas exchange"
        IF `this Subdivision applies to the offer` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "then this Division does not apply to that offer"
        IF (`this Subdivision applies to the offer` EQUALS NOTHING) OR (`the securities or contracts of the offer or intended offer are relevant securities or securities-based derivatives contracts` EQUALS NOTHING)
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the answer of another provision (the disapplication of this Subdivision, or the meaning of relevant securities) was not worked out
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

@ref s 240AA(2) (the prohibition as a rule) (src:38846-38862)
GIVEN
    `the person` IS A Party @desc Who is the person who publishes or disseminates the document?
    `what section 240AA(2) answers for the person` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function `s 240AA(2) the person must not publish or disseminate the document` answer for the person? (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE, or NOTHING if you do not know.)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 240AA action`
`s 240AA(2) the person shall not publish or disseminate the document` MEANS
    IF `what section 240AA(2) answers for the person` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN PARTY `the person`
         SHANT `s 240AA(2) publish or disseminate the document`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY `the person` BECAUSE "the document that resembles a product highlights sheet was published or disseminated; section 240AA(4) makes that an offence"
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- s 240AA(3): the Authority may publish a lodged product highlights sheet. A power with no gate, limited by its own object.
-- src:38866 | (3) The Authority may, for public information, publish —
-- src:38868 | (a) a product highlights sheet lodged with the Authority under
-- src:38869 | this section; and
-- src:38871 | (b) where applicable, the translation thereof in the English
-- src:38872 | language lodged with the Authority under section 318A(1).
@ref s 240AA(3) (src:38866-38872)
GIVEN
    `the document is a product highlights sheet lodged with the Authority under section 240AA` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the document a product highlights sheet lodged with the Authority under section 240AA?
    `the document is the English translation of a product highlights sheet, lodged with the Authority under section 318A(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the document the English translation of a product highlights sheet, lodged with the Authority under section 318A(1)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 240AA(3) the Authority may publish the document for public information` MEANS
    IF `the document is a product highlights sheet lodged with the Authority under section 240AA` OR `the document is the English translation of a product highlights sheet, lodged with the Authority under section 318A(1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The Authority may, for public information, publish (a) a product highlights sheet lodged with the Authority under this section; and (b) where applicable, the translation thereof in the English language lodged with the Authority under section 318A(1)"

-- s 240AA(4): the offence of contravening (1) or (2), and its penalty.
-- src:38876 | (4) Any person who contravenes subsection (1) or (2) shall be
-- src:38877 | guilty of an offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not
-- src:38878 | exceeding $50,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding
-- src:38879 | 12 months or to both and, in the case of a continuing offence, to a
-- src:38880 | further fine not exceeding $5,000 for every day or part of a day during
-- src:38881 | which the offence continues after conviction.
@ref s 240AA(4) (src:38876-38881)
GIVEN
    `what section 240AA(1) answers for the person` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function `s 240AA(1) the person must not make the offer` answer for the person? (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE, or NOTHING if you do not know.)
    `what section 240AA(2) answers for the person` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function `s 240AA(2) the person must not publish or disseminate the document` answer for the person? (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE, or NOTHING if you do not know.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
-- FORK F12 (see NOTES.md, Fork register)
`s 240AA(4) the person is guilty of an offence` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (`what section 240AA(1) answers for the person` EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR (`what section 240AA(2) answers for the person` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF (`what section 240AA(1) answers for the person` EQUALS JUST FALSE) AND (`what section 240AA(2) answers for the person` EQUALS JUST FALSE)
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Any person who contravenes subsection (1) or (2) shall be guilty of an offence"  -- SPLIT-SITE (i)
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): an answer under subsection (1) or (2) was not worked out

@ref s 240AA(4) (the penalty) (src:38876-38881)
GIVETH A Penalty
`s 240AA(4) the penalty for the offence` MEANS
    Penalty OF 50000, 12, TRUE, 5000  -- a fine not exceeding $50,000, or imprisonment not exceeding 12 months, or both; a further fine not exceeding $5,000 for every day or part of a day the offence continues after conviction

§ `s 240AA(5): the definitions`

-- "asset-backed securities" has the meaning given by section 262(3), which lies outside this range (seam S5): the answer of that provision is passed through as it is.
-- src:38890 | “asset‑backed securities” has the meaning given by
-- src:38891 | section 262(3);
@ref s 240AA(5) "asset-backed securities" (src:38890-38891)
GIVEN
    `the securities are asset-backed securities as section 262(3) defines them` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does section 262(3) (the meaning of "asset-backed securities") answer for the securities? (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE, or NOTHING if you do not know.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 240AA(5) "asset-backed securities" the securities are asset-backed securities` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the securities are asset-backed securities as section 262(3) defines them` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the securities are asset-backed securities as section 262(3) defines them` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "has the meaning given by section 262(3)" -- the answer of section 262(3), whose text is another part's range, is passed through as it is
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the meaning is given by section 262(3), and its answer was not worked out

-- "relevant securities or securities-based derivatives contracts" means three things. "means" closes the definition; the third is a prescription, taken as a fact.
-- src:38893 | “relevant securities or securities‑based derivatives contracts”
-- src:38894 | means —
-- src:38896 | (a) asset‑backed securities;
-- src:38898 | (b) structured notes; or
-- src:38900 | (c) such other securities or securities‑based derivatives
-- src:38901 | contracts as the Authority may prescribe by
-- src:38902 | regulations made under section 341;
@ref s 240AA(5) "relevant securities or securities-based derivatives contracts" (src:38893-38902)
GIVEN
    `the securities or contracts are asset-backed securities` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function `s 240AA(5) "asset-backed securities" the securities are asset-backed securities` answer for the securities or contracts? (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE, or NOTHING if you do not know.)
    `the securities or contracts are structured notes` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function `s 240AA(5) "structured notes" the debentures or units of debentures are structured notes` answer for the securities or contracts? (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE, or NOTHING if you do not know.)
    `the Authority has prescribed the securities or contracts as relevant by regulations made under section 341` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Authority prescribed, by regulations made under section 341, that these securities or securities-based derivatives contracts are relevant securities or securities-based derivatives contracts?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 240AA(5) "relevant securities or securities-based derivatives contracts" the securities or contracts are relevant` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (`the securities or contracts are asset-backed securities` EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR (`the securities or contracts are structured notes` EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR `the Authority has prescribed the securities or contracts as relevant by regulations made under section 341`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF (`the securities or contracts are asset-backed securities` EQUALS JUST FALSE) AND (`the securities or contracts are structured notes` EQUALS JUST FALSE)
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "relevant securities or securities-based derivatives contracts means (a) asset-backed securities; (b) structured notes; or (c) such other securities or securities-based derivatives contracts as the Authority may prescribe by regulations made under section 341"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): an answer for asset-backed securities or structured notes was not worked out

-- "single purpose vehicle" means an entity or a trust established solely for the purposes in (a) or (b). "means" and "solely" close it.
-- src:38904 | “single purpose vehicle” means an entity that is established
-- src:38905 | solely in order to, or a trust that is established solely in order
-- src:38906 | for its trustee to, do either or both of the following:
-- src:38908 | (a) act as counterparty to arrangements which involve
-- src:38909 | the use of derivatives to create exposure to assets
-- src:38910 | from which payments to holders of any structured
-- src:38911 | notes are or will be primarily derived;
-- src:38913 | (b) issue any structured notes;
@ref s 240AA(5) "single purpose vehicle" (src:38904-38913)
GIVEN
    `the body is an entity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the body an entity (as section 2(1) defines "entity")?
    `the body is a trust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the body a trust?
    `the body is established in order to act as counterparty to arrangements which involve the use of derivatives to create exposure to assets from which payments to holders of any structured notes are or will be primarily derived` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the body (or, for a trust, the trust for its trustee to) established in order to act as counterparty to arrangements that involve the use of derivatives to create exposure to assets from which payments to holders of any structured notes are or will be primarily derived?
    `the body is established in order to issue any structured notes` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the body (or, for a trust, the trust for its trustee to) established in order to issue any structured notes?
    `the body is established for no purpose other than those` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the body established for no purpose other than acting as counterparty as described, issuing structured notes, or both?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 240AA(5) "single purpose vehicle" the body is a single purpose vehicle` MEANS
    IF (`the body is an entity` OR `the body is a trust`) AND (`the body is established in order to act as counterparty to arrangements which involve the use of derivatives to create exposure to assets from which payments to holders of any structured notes are or will be primarily derived` OR `the body is established in order to issue any structured notes`) AND `the body is established for no purpose other than those`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "single purpose vehicle means an entity that is established solely in order to, or a trust that is established solely in order for its trustee to, do either or both of the following"

-- "specified financial institution" means a licensed bank or an entity the Authority has specified by notification in the Gazette.
-- src:38915 | “specified financial institution” means —
-- src:38917 | (a) any bank licensed under the Banking Act 1970; or
-- src:38919 | (b) any entity that is, or that belongs to a class of entities
-- src:38920 | that is, specified by the Authority, by notification in
-- src:38921 | the Gazette, to be an entity, or a class of entities, for
-- src:38922 | the purposes of this definition;
@ref s 240AA(5) "specified financial institution" (src:38915-38922)
GIVEN
    `the body is a bank licensed under the Banking Act 1970` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the body a bank licensed under the Banking Act 1970?
    `the body is an entity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the body an entity (as section 2(1) defines "entity")?
    `the Authority has specified the body, or a class of entities to which it belongs, by notification in the Gazette for the purposes of this definition` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Authority, by notification in the Gazette, specified the body, or a class of entities to which the body belongs, as a specified financial institution?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 240AA(5) "specified financial institution" the body is a specified financial institution` MEANS
    IF `the body is a bank licensed under the Banking Act 1970` OR (`the body is an entity` AND `the Authority has specified the body, or a class of entities to which it belongs, by notification in the Gazette for the purposes of this definition`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "specified financial institution means (a) any bank licensed under the Banking Act 1970; or (b) any entity that is, or that belongs to a class of entities that is, specified by the Authority, by notification in the Gazette"

-- "synthetic securitisation transaction" means an arrangement using derivatives to create exposure to assets that are outside a single purpose vehicle.
-- src:38981 | “synthetic securitisation transaction” means an arrangement
-- src:38982 | involving the use of derivatives to create or replicate
-- src:38987 | exposure to assets that are not transferred to, or are not a part
-- src:38988 | of an asset pool held by, a single purpose vehicle.
@ref s 240AA(5) "synthetic securitisation transaction" (src:38981-38988)
GIVEN
    `the arrangement involves the use of derivatives to create or replicate exposure to assets` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the arrangement involve the use of derivatives to create or replicate exposure to assets?
    `the assets are transferred to, or are a part of an asset pool held by, a vehicle` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the assets transferred to, or are they a part of an asset pool held by, a vehicle?
    `the vehicle is a single purpose vehicle` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function `s 240AA(5) "single purpose vehicle" the body is a single purpose vehicle` answer for that vehicle? (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE, or NOTHING if you do not know.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 240AA(5) "synthetic securitisation transaction" the arrangement is a synthetic securitisation transaction` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the arrangement involves the use of derivatives to create or replicate exposure to assets`)
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "synthetic securitisation transaction means an arrangement involving the use of derivatives to create or replicate exposure to assets"
        IF (NOT `the assets are transferred to, or are a part of an asset pool held by, a vehicle`) OR (`the vehicle is a single purpose vehicle` EQUALS JUST FALSE)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the vehicle is a single purpose vehicle` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "exposure to assets that are not transferred to, or are not a part of an asset pool held by, a single purpose vehicle"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the answer for the vehicle was not worked out

-- "structured notes": the chapeau says "any type of debentures or units of debentures"; (a), (b) and the formula tail are then limbs, and the combiner joins them (fork F13 on the tail).
-- src:38924 | “structured notes” means any type of debentures or units of
-- src:38925 | debentures —
@ref s 240AA(5) "structured notes" (src:38924-38925)
GIVEN
    `the instrument is a debenture or a unit of debentures` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the instrument a debenture or a unit of debentures?
    `the debentures are issued in relation to an arrangement, and by an institution, as paragraph (a) describes` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function `s 240AA(5) "structured notes" (a) the debentures are issued in relation to a transaction and by a specified financial institution` answer for the debentures? (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE, or NOTHING if you do not know.)
    `the debentures carry a payment or delivery term as paragraph (b) describes` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function `s 240AA(5) "structured notes" (b) the debentures carry a payment or delivery term` answer for the debentures? (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE, or NOTHING if you do not know.)
    `the payment or delivery follows a formula as the tail of the definition describes` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function `s 240AA(5) "structured notes" in accordance with a formula based on one or more of the variables` answer for the debentures? (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE, or NOTHING if you do not know.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
-- FORK F13 (see NOTES.md, Fork register)
`s 240AA(5) "structured notes" the debentures or units of debentures are structured notes` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the instrument is a debenture or a unit of debentures`)
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "structured notes means any type of debentures or units of debentures"
        IF (`the debentures are issued in relation to an arrangement, and by an institution, as paragraph (a) describes` EQUALS JUST FALSE) OR (`the debentures carry a payment or delivery term as paragraph (b) describes` EQUALS JUST FALSE) OR (`the payment or delivery follows a formula as the tail of the definition describes` EQUALS JUST FALSE)
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "structured notes means any type of debentures or units of debentures (a) which is issued ... and (b) for which ... in accordance with a formula based on one or more of the following"
        IF (`the debentures are issued in relation to an arrangement, and by an institution, as paragraph (a) describes` EQUALS JUST TRUE) AND (`the debentures carry a payment or delivery term as paragraph (b) describes` EQUALS JUST TRUE) AND (`the payment or delivery follows a formula as the tail of the definition describes` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): an answer for one of the limbs was not worked out

-- (a): the raw text reads "(i) in relation to (A) ...; or (B) ...; or (ii) by a specified financial institution; and (b)": three alternatives joined by "or" (fork F21).
-- src:38927 | (a) which is issued —
-- src:38929 | (i) in relation to —
-- src:38931 | (A) a synthetic securitisation transaction; or
-- src:38933 | (B) such other arrangement or transaction as
-- src:38934 | the Authority may prescribe by
-- src:38935 | regulations made under section 341; or
-- src:38940 | (ii) by a specified financial institution; and
@ref s 240AA(5) "structured notes" (a) (src:38927-38940)
GIVEN
    `the debentures are issued in relation to a synthetic securitisation transaction` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function `s 240AA(5) "synthetic securitisation transaction" the arrangement is a synthetic securitisation transaction` answer for the arrangement in relation to which the debentures are issued? (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE, or NOTHING if you do not know.)
    `the debentures are issued in relation to another arrangement or transaction that the Authority has prescribed by regulations made under section 341` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the debentures issued in relation to another arrangement or transaction that the Authority has prescribed by regulations made under section 341?
    `the debentures are issued by a specified financial institution` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function `s 240AA(5) "specified financial institution" the body is a specified financial institution` answer for the body that issues the debentures? (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE, or NOTHING if you do not know.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
-- FORK F21 (see NOTES.md, Fork register)
`s 240AA(5) "structured notes" (a) the debentures are issued in relation to a transaction and by a specified financial institution` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (`the debentures are issued in relation to a synthetic securitisation transaction` EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR `the debentures are issued in relation to another arrangement or transaction that the Authority has prescribed by regulations made under section 341` OR (`the debentures are issued by a specified financial institution` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF (`the debentures are issued in relation to a synthetic securitisation transaction` EQUALS JUST FALSE) AND (NOT `the debentures are issued in relation to another arrangement or transaction that the Authority has prescribed by regulations made under section 341`) AND (`the debentures are issued by a specified financial institution` EQUALS JUST FALSE)
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(a) which is issued (i) in relation to (A) a synthetic securitisation transaction; or (B) such other arrangement or transaction as the Authority may prescribe by regulations made under section 341; or (ii) by a specified financial institution"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): an answer for the transaction or the institution was not worked out

-- (b)(i) to (iv): what is payable or delivered. (iv) "2 or more of sub-paragraphs (i), (ii) and (iii) apply" adds nothing to the "or" of (i), (ii) and (iii); it is computed so the text is followed.
-- src:38942 | (b) for which —
-- src:38944 | (i) the principal sum or any interest is, or both are,
-- src:38945 | payable;
-- src:38947 | (ii) such other sum or sums as the Authority may
-- src:38948 | prescribe by regulations made under
-- src:38949 | section 341, is or are payable;
-- src:38951 | (iii) one or more underlying assets, being securities
-- src:38952 | or securities‑based derivatives contracts, equity
-- src:38953 | interests, commodities, currencies or such
-- src:38954 | other assets as the Authority may prescribe
-- src:38955 | by regulations made under section 341, are to
-- src:38956 | be physically delivered; or
-- src:38958 | (iv) 2 or more of sub‑paragraphs (i), (ii) and (iii)
-- src:38959 | apply,
@ref s 240AA(5) "structured notes" (b) (src:38942-38959)
GIVEN
    `the principal sum is payable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the principal sum payable on the debentures?
    `any interest is payable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is any interest payable on the debentures?
    `such other sum or sums as the Authority has prescribed by regulations made under section 341 is or are payable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is any other sum payable that the Authority has prescribed by regulations made under section 341?
    `one or more underlying assets are to be physically delivered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are one or more underlying assets, being securities or securities-based derivatives contracts, equity interests, commodities, currencies or such other assets as the Authority has prescribed by regulations made under section 341, to be physically delivered?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 240AA(5) "structured notes" (b) the debentures carry a payment or delivery term` MEANS
    IF (`the principal sum is payable` OR `any interest is payable`) OR `such other sum or sums as the Authority has prescribed by regulations made under section 341 is or are payable` OR `one or more underlying assets are to be physically delivered` OR (((`the principal sum is payable` OR `any interest is payable`) AND `such other sum or sums as the Authority has prescribed by regulations made under section 341 is or are payable`) OR ((`the principal sum is payable` OR `any interest is payable`) AND `one or more underlying assets are to be physically delivered`) OR (`such other sum or sums as the Authority has prescribed by regulations made under section 341 is or are payable` AND `one or more underlying assets are to be physically delivered`))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) for which (i) the principal sum or any interest is, or both are, payable; (ii) such other sum or sums as the Authority may prescribe by regulations made under section 341, is or are payable; (iii) one or more underlying assets, being securities or securities-based derivatives contracts, equity interests, commodities, currencies or such other assets as the Authority may prescribe by regulations made under section 341, are to be physically delivered; or (iv) 2 or more of sub-paragraphs (i), (ii) and (iii) apply"

-- The tail "(b) in accordance with a formula based on one or more of the following" (the rendering numbers its four variables (v) to (viii)); read as qualifying the whole of paragraph (b) (fork F13).
-- src:38961 | (b) in accordance with a formula based on one or more of
-- src:38962 | the following:
-- src:38964 | (v) the performance of any type of securities or
-- src:38965 | securities‑based derivatives contracts, equity
-- src:38966 | interest, commodity or index, or of a basket of 2
-- src:38967 | or more types of securities or securities‑based
-- src:38968 | derivatives contracts, equity interests,
-- src:38969 | commodities or indices;
-- src:38971 | (vi) the credit risk or performance of any entity or a
-- src:38972 | basket of entities;
-- src:38974 | (vii) the movement of interest rates or currency
-- src:38975 | exchange rates;
-- src:38977 | (viii) such other variables as the Authority may
-- src:38978 | prescribe by regulations made under
-- src:38979 | section 341;
@ref s 240AA(5) "structured notes" in accordance with a formula based on one or more of the variables (src:38961-38979)
GIVEN
    `the formula is based on the performance of any type of securities or securities-based derivatives contracts, equity interest, commodity or index, or of a basket of 2 or more of them` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the formula based on the performance of any type of securities or securities-based derivatives contracts, equity interest, commodity or index, or of a basket of 2 or more types of them?
    `the formula is based on the credit risk or performance of any entity or a basket of entities` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the formula based on the credit risk or performance of any entity or a basket of entities?
    `the formula is based on the movement of interest rates or currency exchange rates` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the formula based on the movement of interest rates or currency exchange rates?
    `the formula is based on such other variables as the Authority has prescribed by regulations made under section 341` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the formula based on such other variables as the Authority has prescribed by regulations made under section 341?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 240AA(5) "structured notes" in accordance with a formula based on one or more of the variables` MEANS
    IF `the formula is based on the performance of any type of securities or securities-based derivatives contracts, equity interest, commodity or index, or of a basket of 2 or more of them` OR `the formula is based on the credit risk or performance of any entity or a basket of entities` OR `the formula is based on the movement of interest rates or currency exchange rates` OR `the formula is based on such other variables as the Authority has prescribed by regulations made under section 341`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in accordance with a formula based on one or more of the following (v) the performance of any type of securities or securities-based derivatives contracts, equity interest, commodity or index, or of a basket of 2 or more types of securities or securities-based derivatives contracts, equity interests, commodities or indices; (vi) the credit risk or performance of any entity or a basket of entities; (vii) the movement of interest rates or currency exchange rates; (viii) such other variables as the Authority may prescribe by regulations made under section 341"

§ `s 240AB: exemption from the product highlights sheet requirement`

DECLARE `s 240AB action` IS ONE OF
    `s 240AB(5) contravene the condition or restriction`

-- s 240AB(1) and (2): the Authority's exemption, by regulations or by written notice. The text says when the Authority may exempt and says nothing of a person it has not exempted.
-- src:38994 | 240AB.—(1) Despite section 337(1), the Authority may, by
-- src:38995 | regulations made under section 341, exempt any person or class of
-- src:38996 | persons from all or any of the requirements in section 240AA, subject
-- src:38997 | to such conditions or restrictions as the Authority may specify.
-- src:39001 | (2) The Authority may, by written notice, exempt any person from
-- src:39002 | all or any of the requirements in section 240AA, subject to such
-- src:39003 | conditions or restrictions as the Authority may specify by written
-- src:39004 | notice.
@ref s 240AB(1) and (2) (src:38994-39004)
GIVEN
    `the Authority has by regulations made under section 341 exempted the person, or a class of persons to which the person belongs` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Authority, by regulations made under section 341, exempted the person, or a class of persons to which the person belongs, from all or any of the requirements in section 240AA?
    `the Authority has by written notice exempted the person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Authority, by written notice, exempted the person from all or any of the requirements in section 240AA?
    `the exemption extends to the requirement the person is asked about` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the exemption extend to the requirement in section 240AA that the person is asked about (the exemption may be from all or any of the requirements)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 240AB(1) and (2) the person is exempt from the requirements in section 240AA` MEANS
    IF (`the Authority has by regulations made under section 341 exempted the person, or a class of persons to which the person belongs` OR `the Authority has by written notice exempted the person`) AND `the exemption extends to the requirement the person is asked about`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the Authority may, by regulations made under section 341, exempt any person or class of persons from all or any of the requirements in section 240AA"; "The Authority may, by written notice, exempt any person from all or any of the requirements in section 240AA"

-- s 240AB(3): the Authority may at any time add to, vary or revoke a condition. A revoked condition no longer binds.
-- src:39008 | (3) The Authority may at any time add to, vary or revoke any
-- src:39009 | condition or restriction imposed under subsection (1) or (2).
@ref s 240AB(3) (src:39008-39009)
GIVEN
    `the Authority has imposed, added or varied the condition or restriction under subsection (1), (2) or (3)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Authority imposed the condition or restriction under section 240AB(1) or (2), or added it or varied it under section 240AB(3)?
    `the Authority has revoked the condition or restriction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Authority revoked the condition or restriction?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 240AB(3) the condition or restriction is in force` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the Authority has imposed, added or varied the condition or restriction under subsection (1), (2) or (3)`)
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any condition or restriction imposed under subsection (1) or (2)"
        IF `the Authority has revoked the condition or restriction`
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The Authority may at any time add to, vary or revoke any condition or restriction imposed under subsection (1) or (2)"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- s 240AB(4): a flat negative on the Gazette.
-- src:39013 | (4) It is not necessary to publish any exemption granted under
-- src:39014 | subsection (2) in the Gazette.
@ref s 240AB(4) (src:39013-39014)
GIVEN
    `the exemption was granted under subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the exemption granted by written notice under section 240AB(2)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 240AB(4) it is necessary to publish the exemption in the Gazette` MEANS
    IF `the exemption was granted under subsection (2)`
    THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "It is not necessary to publish any exemption granted under subsection (2) in the Gazette"
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any exemption granted under subsection (2)" says nothing of an exemption by regulations under subsection (1)

-- s 240AB(5): the offence of contravening a condition, and its penalty.
-- src:39018 | (5) Any person who contravenes any condition or restriction
-- src:39019 | imposed under subsection (1), (2) or (3) shall be guilty of an
-- src:39020 | offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding
-- src:39021 | $50,000 and, in the case of a continuing offence, to a further fine not
-- src:39022 | exceeding $5,000 for every day or part of a day during which the
-- src:39023 | offence continues after conviction.
@ref s 240AB(5) (src:39018-39023)
GIVEN
    `the person contravenes a condition or restriction imposed under subsection (1), (2) or (3)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person contravene a condition or restriction imposed under section 240AB(1), (2) or (3)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
-- FORK F14 (see NOTES.md, Fork register)
`s 240AB(5) the person is guilty of an offence` MEANS
    IF `the person contravenes a condition or restriction imposed under subsection (1), (2) or (3)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Any person who contravenes any condition or restriction imposed under subsection (1), (2) or (3) shall be guilty of an offence"  -- SPLIT-SITE (i)

@ref s 240AB(5) (the penalty) (src:39018-39023)
GIVETH A Penalty
`s 240AB(5) the penalty for the offence` MEANS
    Penalty OF 50000, 0, FALSE, 5000  -- a fine not exceeding $50,000; no imprisonment is stated (0); a further fine not exceeding $5,000 for every day or part of a day the offence continues after conviction

@ref s 240AB(5) (the prohibition on contravening a condition) (src:39018-39023)
GIVEN
    `the person` IS A Party @desc Who is the person bound by the condition or restriction?
    `what section 240AB(3) answers for the condition or restriction` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function `s 240AB(3) the condition or restriction is in force` answer for the condition or restriction? (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE, or NOTHING if you do not know.)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 240AB action`
`s 240AB(5) the person shall not contravene a condition or restriction` MEANS
    IF `what section 240AB(3) answers for the condition or restriction` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN PARTY `the person`
         SHANT `s 240AB(5) contravene the condition or restriction`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY `the person` BECAUSE "a condition or restriction imposed under section 240AB was contravened, which is an offence under section 240AB(5)"
    ELSE FULFILLED

§ `s 240A: debenture issuance programme`

-- s 240A(1): what the prospectus for every offer of debentures that is part of a debenture issuance programme must comprise. A duty with no breach path of its own.
-- src:39029 | 240A.—(1) A prospectus for every offer of debentures or units of
-- src:39030 | debentures that is part of a debenture issuance programme must
-- src:39031 | comprise —
-- src:39033 | (a) a base prospectus applicable to every offer under the
-- src:39034 | debenture issuance programme; and
-- src:39036 | (b) a pricing statement applicable to that particular offer.
@ref s 240A(1) (src:39029-39036)
GIVEN
    `the offer is an offer of debentures or units of debentures that is part of a debenture issuance programme` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the offer an offer of debentures or units of debentures that is part of a debenture issuance programme?
    `the prospectus comprises a base prospectus applicable to every offer under the debenture issuance programme` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the prospectus comprise a base prospectus applicable to every offer under the debenture issuance programme?
    `the prospectus comprises a pricing statement applicable to that particular offer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the prospectus comprise a pricing statement applicable to that particular offer?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 240A(1) the prospectus comprises what it must comprise` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the offer is an offer of debentures or units of debentures that is part of a debenture issuance programme`)
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A prospectus for every offer of debentures or units of debentures that is part of a debenture issuance programme must comprise"
        IF `the prospectus comprises a base prospectus applicable to every offer under the debenture issuance programme` AND `the prospectus comprises a pricing statement applicable to that particular offer`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must comprise (a) a base prospectus applicable to every offer under the debenture issuance programme; and (b) a pricing statement applicable to that particular offer"

-- s 240A(2): the same for a profile statement.
-- src:39041 | (2) A profile statement for every offer of debentures or units of
-- src:39042 | debentures that is part of a debenture issuance programme must
-- src:39043 | comprise —
-- src:39045 | (a) an extract from, or an abridged version of, a base
-- src:39046 | prospectus referred to in subsection (1)(a) (called in this
-- src:39047 | section a base profile statement); and
-- src:39049 | (b) a pricing statement applicable to that particular offer.
@ref s 240A(2) (src:39041-39049)
GIVEN
    `the offer is an offer of debentures or units of debentures that is part of a debenture issuance programme` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the offer an offer of debentures or units of debentures that is part of a debenture issuance programme?
    `the profile statement comprises an extract from, or an abridged version of, a base prospectus (a base profile statement)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the profile statement comprise an extract from, or an abridged version of, a base prospectus referred to in section 240A(1)(a) (called in section 240A a base profile statement)?
    `the profile statement comprises a pricing statement applicable to that particular offer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the profile statement comprise a pricing statement applicable to that particular offer?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 240A(2) the profile statement comprises what it must comprise` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the offer is an offer of debentures or units of debentures that is part of a debenture issuance programme`)
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A profile statement for every offer of debentures or units of debentures that is part of a debenture issuance programme must comprise"
        IF `the profile statement comprises an extract from, or an abridged version of, a base prospectus (a base profile statement)` AND `the profile statement comprises a pricing statement applicable to that particular offer`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must comprise (a) an extract from, or an abridged version of, a base prospectus referred to in subsection (1)(a) (called in this section a base profile statement); and (b) a pricing statement applicable to that particular offer"

-- s 240A(3): the route for the requirements of s 240(1)(a)(ii) and (iii). "are satisfied if" is a failed "if" when its gate fails (reading (a)).
-- src:39051 | (3) In respect of an offer referred to in subsection (1), the
-- src:39052 | requirements of section 240(1)(a)(ii) and (iii) are satisfied if a copy
-- src:39053 | of the base prospectus and a copy of the pricing statement, each of
-- src:39054 | which is signed in accordance with section 240(4A), have been
-- src:39055 | lodged with and registered by the Authority, either separately,
-- src:39056 | whether on the same date or on different dates, or as a single
-- src:39057 | document.
@ref s 240A(3) (src:39051-39057)
GIVEN
    `the offer is an offer referred to in subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the offer an offer of debentures or units of debentures that is part of a debenture issuance programme (an offer referred to in section 240A(1))?
    `a copy of the base prospectus, signed in accordance with section 240(4A), has been lodged with the Authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a copy of the base prospectus, signed as section 240(4A) requires, been lodged with the Authority?
    `a copy of the pricing statement, signed in accordance with section 240(4A), has been lodged with the Authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a copy of the pricing statement, signed as section 240(4A) requires, been lodged with the Authority?
    `the base prospectus and the pricing statement have each been registered by the Authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the base prospectus and the pricing statement each been registered by the Authority?
    `the copies were lodged and registered as a single document` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were a copy of the base prospectus and a copy of the pricing statement, each signed as section 240(4A) requires, lodged with and registered by the Authority as a single document?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 240A(3) the requirements of section 240(1)(a)(ii) and (iii) are satisfied for the offer` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the offer is an offer referred to in subsection (1)`)
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In respect of an offer referred to in subsection (1), the requirements of section 240(1)(a)(ii) and (iii) are satisfied"
        IF `the copies were lodged and registered as a single document` OR (`a copy of the base prospectus, signed in accordance with section 240(4A), has been lodged with the Authority` AND `a copy of the pricing statement, signed in accordance with section 240(4A), has been lodged with the Authority` AND `the base prospectus and the pricing statement have each been registered by the Authority`)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the requirements of section 240(1)(a)(ii) and (iii) are satisfied if a copy of the base prospectus and a copy of the pricing statement, each of which is signed in accordance with section 240(4A), have been lodged with and registered by the Authority, either separately, whether on the same date or on different dates, or as a single document"  -- MARGINAL-READING (a)

-- s 240A(4): the same for a profile statement and the requirements of s 240(4)(b) and (c).
-- src:39059 | (4) In respect of an offer referred to in subsection (2), the
-- src:39060 | requirements of section 240(4)(b) and (c) are satisfied if a copy of
-- src:39061 | the base profile statement and a copy of the pricing statement, each of
-- src:39062 | which is signed in accordance with section 240(4A), have been
-- src:39063 | lodged with and registered by the Authority, either separately,
-- src:39064 | whether on the same date or on different dates, or as a single
-- src:39065 | document.
@ref s 240A(4) (src:39059-39065)
GIVEN
    `the offer is an offer referred to in subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the offer an offer of debentures or units of debentures that is part of a debenture issuance programme and made with a profile statement (an offer referred to in section 240A(2))?
    `a copy of the base profile statement, signed in accordance with section 240(4A), has been lodged with the Authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a copy of the base profile statement, signed as section 240(4A) requires, been lodged with the Authority?
    `a copy of the pricing statement, signed in accordance with section 240(4A), has been lodged with the Authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a copy of the pricing statement, signed as section 240(4A) requires, been lodged with the Authority?
    `the base profile statement and the pricing statement have each been registered by the Authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the base profile statement and the pricing statement each been registered by the Authority?
    `the copies were lodged and registered as a single document` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were a copy of the base profile statement and a copy of the pricing statement, each signed as section 240(4A) requires, lodged with and registered by the Authority as a single document?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 240A(4) the requirements of section 240(4)(b) and (c) are satisfied for the offer` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the offer is an offer referred to in subsection (2)`)
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In respect of an offer referred to in subsection (2), the requirements of section 240(4)(b) and (c) are satisfied"
        IF `the copies were lodged and registered as a single document` OR (`a copy of the base profile statement, signed in accordance with section 240(4A), has been lodged with the Authority` AND `a copy of the pricing statement, signed in accordance with section 240(4A), has been lodged with the Authority` AND `the base profile statement and the pricing statement have each been registered by the Authority`)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the requirements of section 240(4)(b) and (c) are satisfied if a copy of the base profile statement and a copy of the pricing statement, each of which is signed in accordance with section 240(4A), have been lodged with and registered by the Authority, either separately, whether on the same date or on different dates, or as a single document"  -- MARGINAL-READING (a)

-- s 240A(5): to avoid doubt, a registered base prospectus or base profile statement is treated as lodged and registered for every offer under the programme. A "where" gate: periods ruling of 2026-11-05, rule (b).
-- src:39067 | (5) To avoid doubt, where the base prospectus or base profile
-- src:39068 | statement in relation to a debenture issuance programme has been
-- src:39069 | lodged with and registered by the Authority, it is treated as having
-- src:39070 | been lodged with and registered by the Authority in respect of every
-- src:39071 | offer under that programme.
@ref s 240A(5) (src:39067-39071)
GIVEN
    `the offer is an offer under the debenture issuance programme` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the offer an offer under the debenture issuance programme?
    `the base prospectus or base profile statement in relation to the programme has been lodged with and registered by the Authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the base prospectus or base profile statement in relation to the debenture issuance programme been lodged with and registered by the Authority?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 240A(5) the base prospectus or base profile statement is treated as lodged with and registered by the Authority for the offer` MEANS
    IF `the offer is an offer under the debenture issuance programme` AND `the base prospectus or base profile statement in relation to the programme has been lodged with and registered by the Authority`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where the base prospectus or base profile statement in relation to a debenture issuance programme has been lodged with and registered by the Authority, it is treated as having been lodged with and registered by the Authority in respect of every offer under that programme"  -- MARGINAL-READING (a)

-- s 240A(6): "a reference to a prospectus" is read as both documents, unless the context otherwise requires or the Authority has prescribed otherwise.
-- src:39073 | (6) For the purposes of the application of the provisions of this
-- src:39074 | Subdivision to an offer referred to in subsection (1), a reference to a
-- src:39075 | prospectus is, unless the context otherwise requires or the Authority
-- src:39076 | has prescribed otherwise, to be read as a reference to both the base
-- src:39077 | prospectus and the pricing statement.
@ref s 240A(6) (src:39073-39077)
GIVEN
    `the offer is an offer referred to in subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the offer an offer of debentures or units of debentures that is part of a debenture issuance programme (an offer referred to in section 240A(1))?
    `the context otherwise requires` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the context of the provision in which the reference to a prospectus appears otherwise require?
    `the Authority has prescribed otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Authority prescribed otherwise?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 240A(6) a reference to a prospectus is read as a reference to both the base prospectus and the pricing statement` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the offer is an offer referred to in subsection (1)`)
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "For the purposes of the application of the provisions of this Subdivision to an offer referred to in subsection (1), a reference to a prospectus is"
        IF `the context otherwise requires` OR `the Authority has prescribed otherwise`
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the context otherwise requires or the Authority has prescribed otherwise"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- s 240A(7): the same for a reference to a profile statement.
-- src:39079 | (7) For the purposes of the application of the provisions of this
-- src:39080 | Subdivision to an offer referred to in subsection (2), a reference to a
-- src:39081 | profile statement is, unless the context otherwise requires or the
-- src:39086 | Authority has prescribed otherwise, to be read as a reference to both
-- src:39087 | the base profile statement and the pricing statement.
@ref s 240A(7) (src:39079-39087)
GIVEN
    `the offer is an offer referred to in subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the offer an offer of debentures or units of debentures that is part of a debenture issuance programme and made with a profile statement (an offer referred to in section 240A(2))?
    `the context otherwise requires` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the context of the provision in which the reference to a profile statement appears otherwise require?
    `the Authority has prescribed otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Authority prescribed otherwise?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 240A(7) a reference to a profile statement is read as a reference to both the base profile statement and the pricing statement` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the offer is an offer referred to in subsection (2)`)
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "For the purposes of the application of the provisions of this Subdivision to an offer referred to in subsection (2), a reference to a profile statement is"
        IF `the context otherwise requires` OR `the Authority has prescribed otherwise`
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the context otherwise requires or the Authority has prescribed otherwise"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- s 240A(9): to avoid doubt, a pricing statement may be registered at any time after its lodgment. A "may" gated by a time ("at any time after"): fork F15, split site (ii).
-- src:39093 | (9) To avoid doubt, a pricing statement may be registered by the
-- src:39094 | Authority at any time after its lodgment with the Authority.
@ref s 240A(9) (src:39093-39094)
GIVEN
    `the date the pricing statement is lodged` IS A DATE @desc On what date is the pricing statement lodged with the Authority?
    `the day on which registration is asked about` IS A DATE @desc On what day would the Authority register the pricing statement?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
-- FORK F15 (see NOTES.md, Fork register)
`s 240A(9) the Authority may register the pricing statement on the day` MEANS
    IF `the day on which registration is asked about` AT LEAST `the date the pricing statement is lodged`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a pricing statement may be registered by the Authority at any time after its lodgment with the Authority"  -- SPLIT-SITE (ii)
